d=dataset('planet-irrigation-field-comparison','398','A field trial with an exception',rows,['planet-irrigation'],'water deficit index','Source-derived spatial mean WDI for each field × growth stage × growing season; two fields and two seasons, not eight independent trials','Two corn fields at a central Kansas farm; no national extrapolation',('2021','2023'),'No global water savings, randomized causal estimate, measured crop-yield gain, fertilizer reduction or cross-climate transfer test','Different irrigation hardware and management co-vary with AI use. WDI relies on satellite NDVI and evapotranspiration modelling, not direct field evapotranspiration measurements. In2023vegetative-stage WDI is higher in the AI field; retain this exception. Published p threshold0.1 and descriptive SDs do not cure lack of field replication; the SD aggregation and sample count are not specified in the extracted table.')
audit('398','reframe-ready',[d['datasetId']],'A two-field Kansas comparison reports lower satellite-derived crop water stress under AI-Radar during reproductive stages, but an opposite numerical result in2023vegetative growth.','When does an AI-guided field look less water-stressed, and when does it not?','Use a bounded observational field comparison; AI, hardware and management effects cannot be separated, and transferability remains untested.',search=[m.SOURCES['planet-irrigation']['url'],'https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S277237552600479X','https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-024-76915-8'])

